WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.939 --> 00:00:02.110
Willy.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:07.469
Come to me, come to me in my time of need, hold me. Good morning Hank.

00:00:07.469 --> 00:00:13.160
It's Sunday, some snowy day in December, and today. I'm going to conquer one of my greatest phobias:

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.960
Heights

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.590
Should I let Willy tell this story instead of me telling it?

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.090
Maybe so.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.380
(Sarah): It'll be easier to cope

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.260
Ok, so John recently went to an author party with Scott Westerfeld and Justine Larbalestier

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.599
And they were teasing him about his profound fear of heights

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.580
and they pointed to a table in a hotel room and

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.480
said: "How much would it cost for you to stand on top of that table?"

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.459
So John had to come up with a monetary figure that was high enough that he wouldn't have to stand on the table

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:48.420
but low enough that he wouldn't seem entirely crazy for being unwilling to stand on top of the table, due to his profound fear of heights.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.920
And the number he finally came up with:

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.800
Five thousand dollars.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.040
To which Scott Westerfeld and Justine Larbalestier said:

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.780
"Okay" , and then offered to make a donation of five thousand - but Willy you are supposed to be telling this story,

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.440
not licking - and then offered him a donation of

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.480
$5000 to his favorite charities if he would stand on top of the table.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.200
And then being my courageous owner,

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.200
I'm sure you can imagine what John did next.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:16.640
He completely failed to get on top of the table because he is a gigantic wuss.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.820
But Scott and Justine agreed to extend the deadline of table standing until today, so today

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.260
I am going to stand on top of a table

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.600
for the children.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.760
I mean people are gonna think that I'm literally crazy.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.280
Can we take my pulse for the purposes of showing that I'm legitimately afraid?

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:40.080
[fast breathing]

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.130
What do you think it is?

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:43.480
(Sarah): I don't know, it's high.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:49.840
I don't think getting on the table will be hard at all. I think that standing on the table will be exceptionally hard.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.620
So...

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.040
I guess I just...

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.880
[nervous laughter]

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.400
Yeah, yeah, I can't do it. I liter- , I don't think I can do it, man.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.360
(Sarah): Get on the table.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.380
[quiet giggle from Sarah]

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.420
Oh my God.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.180
I'm going to do it.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.740
I'm going to do it, and then I'm going to, and then I'm going to stand up on the table

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.400
and then I'm going to get right back down.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.720
Okay, can we have another countdown?

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.740
I'm going to-. I'm going to stand up on the table. I'm going to get right back down. I'm gonna go right now.I'm gonna go.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:33.920
I'm up.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.740
F***.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.840
Okay, I´m on the table.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:48.360
Ha ha ha ha ha yes!! [singing] I got on the table! I stood on the table!

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.100
Yess!!!

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.760
FIVE THOUSAND DOLLARS.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.120
Hank, I don't want to brag but I think that today I have shown a lot of, you know,

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.440
physical courage. I have proven once and for all that

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:07.480
nerdfighters are tough. It's like Franklin Delano Roosevelt said, we have nothing to fear but fear itself.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.100
And heights.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.840
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:17.160
Willy! Willy, let's run through the snow together!!

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.280
Oh!

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.960
This way! This way! This way!

